<title>CANADA: Shell Canada Q4 net soars after gain.</title>
<headline>Shell Canada Q4 net soars after gain.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			  1995</p>
<p> Shr			 C$3.05		   C$0.67</p>
<p> Net			342,000		   75,000</p>
<p> Revs		   1,498,000		1,118,000</p>
<p>	   YEAR</p>
<p> Shr			 C$5.30		   C$4.66</p>
<p> Net			595,000		  523,000</p>
<p> Revs		   5,187,000		4,543,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 112,000		  112,000</p>
<p>		  (All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: Shell Canada Ltd said its 1996 earnings included a C$226 million gain from the sale of its chemicals business on December 31, 1996. 1995 earnings included a C$95 million gain from the sale of its polypropylene business.</p>
<p>Earnings from continuing operations totalled C$103 million in the fourth quarter of 1996 and C$60 million in the same period in 1995. Earnings from continuing operations were C$326 million in the full year of 1996 and C$302 million in 1995.</p>
<p>Earnings in 1996 also included an after-tax writedown of C$50 million to integrate Shell's wholly owned private brand marketing subsidiaries.</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
